  "description": "This easy California-style salad with avocado, goat cheese, and walnuts comes together in 15 minutes. A lightly emulsified Greek dressing and smart tossing technique make it restaurant-worthy.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: mesclun mix → spring mix\n\nNotes: For a punchier dressing, Dijon mustard may be substituted for the mayonnaise.\nFeel free to use just red or green bell pepper, if desired.\nCreamy block feta made from sheep's or goat's milk can be substituted for goat cheese.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The dressing can be made and refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 2 days. Bring to room temperature and whisk to recombine before using.",
